# Google Analytics

This is a static site. Tracking lives in `/analytics.js` (GA4 ID `G-2X3VN4X5ST`). Do not paste a second gtag snippet into pages.

## New HTML pages

Load `analytics.js` in `<head>` after the stylesheet. Match the path depth of that page’s other root assets:

```html
<script src="/analytics.js"></script>          <!-- site root, e.g. index.html -->
<script src="../analytics.js"></script>        <!-- one level, e.g. books/index.html -->
<script src="../../analytics.js"></script>     <!-- two levels, e.g. games/manna-mover/index.html -->
```

## New games

Fire a play event at the top of `startGame()` only from the menu or game-over screen, before `state` changes. Do not fire on day/level transitions.

```js
if (
  typeof window.trackGamePlay === 'function' &&
  (state === 'menu' || state === 'gameOver')
) {
  window.trackGamePlay(
    'Game Display Name',
    state === 'gameOver' ? 'restart' : 'start',
  );
}
```

Use the public game title. `start` is the first play from the menu; `restart` is play-again after game over.

Do not change `MEASUREMENT_ID` or add new event names unless asked. New event parameters must also be registered in GA4 as custom dimensions. Never send Analytics from localhost; `analytics.js` skips `localhost`, `127.0.0.1`, and `file:`.
